//! Field codes: one constant per row of the field catalogue (03-api-model.md §9.1;
//! API-082, GEN-041).
//!
//! An [`Error`](crate::Error) names the field it refers to with one of these constants,
//! and the C ABI carries its code (CABI-021). Codes are never renumbered or reused. The
//! name is for display only and is never compared. Every constant lives here, generated
//! from the catalogue; a codec crate re-exports the constants it uses, so a constant never
//! moves when a second crate starts to use its field (M2 plan D2).
//!
//! A `field` names a field of a data unit defined by a Blue Book; a `parameter` names a
//! managed parameter, a configuration value, an argument, or a length the caller passes.

